.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt ERR_LOAD_CRYPTO_STRINGS 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ERR_load_crypto_strings ,
.Nm SSL_load_error_strings ,
.Nm ERR_free_strings
.Nd load and free error strings
.Sh SYNOPSIS
The following functions have been deprecated since OpenSSL 1.1.0, and
can be hidden entirely by defining
.Ar OPENSSL_API_COMPAT
with a suitable version value, see
.Xr openssl_user_macros 7 :
.In openssl/err.h
.Ft void
.Fo ERR_load_crypto_strings
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo ERR_free_strings
.Fa void
.Fc
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Ft void
.Fo SSL_load_error_strings
.Fa void
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn ERR_load_crypto_strings
registers the error strings for all
.Sy libcrypto
functions.
.Fn SSL_load_error_strings
does the same, but also registers the
.Sy libssl
error strings.
.Pp
In versions prior to OpenSSL 1.1.0,
.Fn ERR_free_strings
releases any resources created by the above functions.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn ERR_load_crypto_strings ,
.Fn SSL_load_error_strings
and
.Fn ERR_free_strings
return no values.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_error_string 3
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn ERR_load_crypto_strings ,
.Fn SSL_load_error_strings ,
and
.Fn ERR_free_strings
functions were deprecated in OpenSSL 1.1.0 by
.Xr OPENSSL_init_crypto 3
and
.Xr OPENSSL_init_ssl 3
and should not be used.
